## Section 3 — Component interfaces (the public shape of each internal package)

### `internal/registry`

```go
type Registry struct {
    client *client.Client
    cache  Cache
}

type Cache interface {
    Get(api.Module) ([]byte, bool, error)
    Put(api.Module, []byte) error
}

func New(c *client.Client, cache Cache) *Registry

// Fetch returns the gzipped tarball bytes for one module version, cache-first.
func (r *Registry) Fetch(ctx context.Context, m api.Module) ([]byte, error)

// FetchPair fans Fetch out concurrently; cancels both on first error.
func (r *Registry) FetchPair(ctx context.Context, a, b api.Module) (aBytes, bBytes []byte, err error)
```

`Cache` is a small interface so tests inject `memCache{}`; production uses `diskCache{dir}`.

### `internal/archive`

```go
// Module is the in-memory representation of an extracted tarball.
// Keys are forward-slash relative paths; symlinks are resolved or rejected.
type Module struct {
    Files map[string][]byte
}

func Extract(tarball []byte, maxBytes int64) (Module, error)
```

`maxBytes` guards against gzip bombs (default 50MB). Symlinks pointing outside the archive root are rejected with an error — standard untar hardening.

### `internal/diff`

```go
type FileDiff struct {
    Path     string
    Status   FileStatus  // Added | Removed | Modified | Renamed (renames detected by content hash; v1 can skip and just report Added+Removed)
    Unified  string      // pre-rendered unified diff (gotextdiff output)
    Adds     int
    Dels     int
}

type ModuleSummary struct {
    Resources map[string]hcl.Block  // key = "type.name"
    Variables map[string]hcl.Block
    Outputs   map[string]hcl.Block
    Providers map[string]hcl.Block
    Locals    map[string]hcl.Block
    Data      map[string]hcl.Block
    Modules   map[string]hcl.Block
}

type SemanticChange struct {
    Kind   string  // "resource" | "variable" | ...
    Name   string
    Status FileStatus
    Detail string  // optional human description of what changed
}

type Result struct {
    Files    []FileDiff       // always populated
    Semantic []SemanticChange // populated only when --semantic
}

func Textual(a, b archive.Module) []FileDiff
func Semantic(a, b archive.Module) ([]SemanticChange, error)
```

v1 keeps `Status: Renamed` out — keeps the heuristic out of scope. We can add it later by hashing identical-content adds/removes.

### `internal/tui`

```go
// Run launches the full TUI starting from a picker; returns final exit error.
func Run(ctx context.Context, reg *registry.Registry, initial api.ModuleIdentifier) error

// RunBrowser launches just the diff browser with a pre-computed Result.
func RunBrowser(ctx context.Context, result diff.Result) error
```

Two entry points so the one-shot path can skip the picker entirely. Both return when user hits `q`. The Model graph is a single `tea.Model` with an internal state enum (`statePickModule | statePickVersionA | statePickVersionB | stateLoading | stateBrowser`) — no nested bubbletea programs.

### `cmd` package

```go
type diffOpts struct {
    CrowURL  string
    Timeout  time.Duration
    Semantic bool
    Plain    bool
    JSON     bool
    CacheDir string
}

func newDiffCmd() *cobra.Command   // returns configured cobra.Command
func newRootCmd() *cobra.Command   // wires global flags + subcommands
```

Functions return `*cobra.Command` instead of using package-level vars — easier to test (each test builds a fresh command tree, no flag-state leakage between tests).

Want me to push on any interface, or move on to error handling + testing?

