The `nil` returned msg is a no-op — bubbletea handles `nil` cleanly. We don't care about the result.

Picker gets a new field `knownPath string`, set from a fourth arg added to `NewPicker(ctx, deps, suggestions, knownPath)`. (So actually `NewPicker(ctx, deps, suggestions, knownPath)` — 4 params. Worth flagging now.)

Acceptable, or do you want the picker to receive a smaller "config" struct instead of 4 positional args?

